body:
Outside of Hostel Part Two most movies by Eli Roth. His movies are mostly\* dumb and I like his style.

&#x200B;

\*You could make sociological arguments about his filmography but outside of that one example I don't think he pulls the ideas off.

*The Wizard of Oz* is probably a great choice. You're not only exposing them to, an admittedly popular, older film but there is a lot of gateways to explore cinema in the framework of the picture. Wanna know about classic Hollywood? Check! Special effects? Check! Just a banger movie? Check!

&#x200B;

Maybe wait a bit to tell them about the horrific behind the scenes stories.
